embering what it would impoverish us to forget.”</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/david_perell/status/1894803964534681970">https://x.com/david_perell/status/1894803964534681970</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/thursday-assorted-links-491.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=thursday-assorted-links-491">Thursday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/david_perell/status/1894803964534681970</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/david_perell/status/1894803964534681970</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Feb 2025 17:09:06 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tax increase pending on Harvard?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GkrNiIgXUAAPWOh.jpg:large"></p><p>Matt Blackwell (@matt_blackwell) on X</p><p>I completely missed that Republicans introduced a bill to increase the endowment tax from 1.4% to 21%. If passed, Harvard would go from paying ~$35m to $525m/yr in federal taxes (that’s 8.2% of its current operating expenses)</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/matt_blackwell/status/1894552583013834892?s=46&t=Az2N-uf1-Lg_ahOy8usSug">https://x.com/matt_blackwell/status/1894552583013834892?s=46&t=Az2N-uf1-Lg_ahOy8usSug</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/thursday-assorted-links-491.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=thursday-assorted-links-491">Thursday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/matt_blackwell/status/1894552583013834892?s=46&amp;t=Az2N-uf1-Lg_ahOy8usSug</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/matt_blackwell/status/1894552583013834892?s=46&amp;t=Az2N-uf1-Lg_ahOy8usSug</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Feb 2025 17:09:06 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[New set of NBER economics papers on AI and economics]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.nber.org/books-and-chapters/economics-artificial-intelligence-political-economy">https://www.nber.org